
1. RUN: insert into runs(run_type, trigger_id, session_id, data_as_of, model, skill_version) returning id. skill_version = 'YYYY-MM-DD-' || first 8 hex of sha256(SKILL.md) using the SKILL.md file's modified date; insert into skill_versions if missing (on conflict do nothing).
2. SIGNALS: insert one row per verdict you give, for EVERY name you give a verdict on (ENTRY, ENTRY_REDUCED, WAIT, WAIT_ALERT, NO_GO, TRIM, ADD, HOLD, REDUCE, EXIT). Never update or delete signals (table blocks it); to correct one, insert a new row with supersedes = old id. Fill: symbol, signal_date (date of the price data the call is based on; weekly scans = the Friday close), source, verdict, provisional (true for every mid-week call unless stop-based), setup, stage, why_grade, why_text, signal_close, pivot, alert_trigger, entry_low/entry_high (entry zone), stop, stop_basis, trim_price, size_pct (planned % of capital; ENTRY_REDUCED = half), risk_pct ((close-stop)/close*100), vol_mult, req_vol_mult, req_vol_abs, sma13, sma13_rising, dist_sma_pct, correction_pct, base_range_pct, close_loc, liquidity_tier ('thin' if median daily traded value < Rs 5 cr), priority_rank, window_start/window_end (entry window: next session through the session before the next weekly scan), skill_version, run_id, notes. For holdings management, HOLD/TRIM/etc. may carry a raised stop in stop (stops are never lowered).
3. PRICES: upsert daily bars into price_bars(symbol, bar_date, open, high, low, close, volume, source) for every symbol with a pending/open position (select symbol from positions where status in ('pending','open')) plus this run's new ENTRY names, from the day after the latest stored bar through the last completed session. Prefer Kite get_historical_data (day interval) when logged in; else Tapetide get_price_history. Budget: at most 20 price calls for the tracker; open/pending positions first, then WAIT_ALERT names from the last 4 weeks (for counterfactual tracking). Before inserting, check the last close matches the quote/screener (transcription check).
4. PROCESS: select process_ledger('<last completed session date>'); the database computes fills, stops, trims, exits, marks and P&L. Never compute or write positions/events/marks yourself.
5. REVIEW: read v_trade_stats, v_open_positions, v_pnl_monthly and v_signal_outcomes; insert one reviews row (period weekly on Fridays, adhoc otherwise) with stats jsonb, observations, lessons. Skill changes go only into reviews.proposed_change with proposal_status 'proposed' and only after min_closed_trades_before_rule_change closed trades in that group; never edit the skill.
6. Close the run: update runs set finished_at=now(), status, data_calls, summary where id = <run id>. Put a short "Paper tracker" table (open positions, P&L to date, events since last run) in the report.
FALLBACK if Supabase tools are not available in the session: write the would-be rows (runs, signals, price_bars) as one JSON file to Google Drive named "tracker-backlog-<YYYY-MM-DD>.json" and say so at the top of the report; the next run that has Supabase ingests every tracker-backlog-*.json not yet ingested (check runs.notes for the file name) and then processes.$p$::text), 'Instructions every scheduled/ad hoc run follows to log into this tracker'),
('fill_rules', to_jsonb($r$Paper fills (computed by process_ledger, replayed from scratch each call): ENTRY/ENTRY_REDUCED non-provisional signals become pending positions. Limit buy at entry_high valid window_start..window_end: fills on the first session whose low <= entry_high at min(open, entry_high); a session opening at/below the stop skips the trade; never filled -> expired. Stop = max(pivot*0.99, fill*0.92). Each later session: management signals dated before it apply at its open (EXIT all, REDUCE half, TRIM trim_fraction once, ADD within the 10% cap); any signal stop above the current stop raises it. Then stop is checked on the daily low (gap below -> fill at open; stop wins when stop and trim both touched), else trim_fraction sold once when the high reaches fill*1.25. Costs: half the round-trip haircut on each side. Skips: max open positions, insufficient cash, already holding.$r$::text), 'Deterministic fill/exit rules');

;
